  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) was only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal and resnet50 image as weak. The biggest uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved. This experiment tests scvi_n200 (a learned, denoised VAE-based representation) versus pca_n2000 (linear) while holding model_setting=rna_only and profile_setting=singleprofile constant, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. If scvi_n200 improves meaningfully over PCA, it justifies investing remaining budget in multiprofile+scvi_n200 and multimodal scvi configurations; if not, we can pivot to scgpt or multiprofile aggregation with PCA. This is the cleanest single-variable comparison available and the best use of experiment 3 to reduce uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

